{"batchcomplete":true,"warnings":{"extracts":{"warnings":"The value "8000" for parameter "exchars" must be between 1 and 1,200."}},"query":{"pages":[{"pageid":39334326,"ns":0,"title":"Judith van Dorth","extract":"Johanna Magdalena Catharina "Judith" van Dorth (7 May 1747, in Warnsveld – 22 November 1799, in Winterswijk), known as Freule Van Dorth (Lady of Dorth), was a Dutch orangist and aristocrat. She was executed for treason. She is the only woman in the history of the Netherlands to have been executed by a military tribunal. She is regarded to have been the victim of terrible injustice, and was used by the orangist political propaganda as a victim of the republicans.


